  "result": "I fixed this in `archiveIssuesForProject` in `src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts`. When a project was archived with its issues, the update touched every issue in the project, including ones already archived. That gave those issues a new archive date and counted them again. It now only updates issues that are still live, and the project filter keeps other projects untouched.\n\nThe count it returns now matches the number of issues actually archived, and that one number feeds the audit-log summary and the usage meter. In the reported case it would be 9, not 12. Before, the meter went down by 12 for only 9 live issues, which is why it read low and at one point went negative. The 4 related test files pass (28 tests), but none of them covers already-archived issues, and I didn't add a test for it.\n\nThe fix only prevents new drift. For workspaces already affected, the meter will be right after the next usage rollup recount, but the archive dates already overwritten can't be restored by this change.",
